      "Events That Must Be Reported",
      "A firm must tell FINRA in writing promptly, and no later than 30 calendar days after it knows or should have known, if the firm or a registered person:\n• Broke any securities law.\n• Is named in a written customer complaint alleging theft, misuse of funds, or forgery.\n• Is sued by a regulator for breaking securities laws.\n• Is denied registration, expelled, suspended, or disciplined by an SRO.\n• Is indicted, convicted, or pleads guilty to any crime. Misdemeanor traffic tickets and misdemeanor DUIs are excluded, but criminal DUIs must be reported.\n• Is tied to a firm that was suspended, expelled, or convicted.\n• Settles a securities or commodities lawsuit or arbitration for more than $15,000, or more than $25,000 if the firm itself is involved.\n• Is subject to statutory disqualification.\n• Is disciplined by the firm with suspension, firing, withheld commissions, or fines over $2,500.",
